project-authored history credits Bu5hm4nn, colmap-parent,
photogram-coordinator and photogram. No separate third-party implementation
or license was present in those terms. No runtime Photogram dependency exists.

This is deliberately a small subset in the SAME eventual product package
location, not a second model namespace or PR16 merge. Future PR16 reconciliation
must retain ONE canonical current-owned-shape helper and route its resident
adapter through that helper rather than retaining two formula authorities.
PR16's frontend, resident parser, file identities, wire and CLI are not copied.
Neither current-phase-v1's resident-only eligibility nor optimized-PHOTO's
qualification is expanded. Fixed-cohort PHOTO and GEO reuse only the exact
current-owned NATIVE LOGICAL MINIMUM inventory, including conservative mask
retention. The added copies/retention/staging terms mirror the base42 runner.

The producer requires observed tight grayscale Bitmap::NumBytes metadata;
non-tight buffers are refused. It preserves all image order, reference order,
phase options, device and duplicate source ordinals. Input pixel/calibration
immutability and actual native invocation validation remain the caller/native
contract; metadata never fabricates file identities or attests pixel contents.

The existing resident allocation generator and digest encoding are reused.
The closure includes the shared native fixed-cohort logical inventory producer;
Python/native parity tests compare its complete raw payload inventory. The
content pin is updated for this implementation, pending independent review.
Content changes refuse until explicit repinning; revision is recorded from
actual Git HEAD, not accepted as a self-whitelisting declaration.

Every field delivered to experimental FixedCohortBudget is RAW. One aggregate
3% margin is applied ONLY by native admission, plus separate explicit headroom.
All caller pixels, frozen copies, both phases' host returns and every PHOTO
snapshot remain charged for the full invocation. GEO staging is already
included in per-job GEO private device storage; it is not charged twice.
Process and positive unknown pitch/array/context/allocator allowance are
explicit caller inputs, not new coefficients or free-minus-known filler.
Classified live-process observation credits remain inside process storage.

This is experimental/unqualified, not calibrated or a hard physical-fit bound.
The tiny fixture's snapshot observation 28672 and staging observations
6144/6144/4608/6144 are NOT calibration and are not model coefficients.
No default dispatch, GPU performance or full-scene qualification is claimed.
The independent installed experimental_fixed_cohort command now uses the shared
native raw producer and existing native workspace/runner/map writers; it does
not require this Python package. See doc/experimental_fixed_cohort.rst. The
generated C++ initializer remains a direct experimental test binding, not a
generic wire framework.

